    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n11389" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Cosmus</span></b> , i, m., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a celebrated maker of,
				and dealer in unguents at Rome</i>, <i><span class="en">Juv. 8,
			86</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Mart. 11, 8, 9</span></i>; <i><span class="en">1, 89, 2</span></i>; <i><span class="en">14, 110,
			1</span></i>.—Hence, <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Cosmĭānus</span></b> , a, um,
				<i>adj., named</i> or <i>derived from
				Cosmus</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ampullae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Mart. 3, 82, 26</span></i>
			; and <i>subst.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Cosmĭānum</span></b> ,
			i, n. (sc. unguentum), <i>an
				unguent made by him</i>, <i><span class="en">Mart. 12,
				55, 7</span></i>; <i><span class="en">11, 15,
				6</span></i>.</div>
